<p style="text-align: center;"><strong><span style="font-size: 12pt;">ARGUMENT IN FAVOR OF<br />
MEASURE RTM<br />
</span></strong></p>
<p style="text-align: left;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Contra Costa County residents depend on a strong regional transit network to keep local residents moving and our economy strong.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Every day, hundreds of thousands of people rely on public transit to get to work, school, medical appointments, and local businesses. Our public transit system reduces traffic, supports the local economy, and ensures everyone has an affordable way to get where they need to go- including families, seniors, people with disabilities, students, and workers.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Today, Bay Area transit faces a turning point. Without new funding from the Regional Transit Measure, we will experience significant and deep cuts to public transit systems including BART, AC Transit, Muni, and Caltrain &#8212; setting us back decades.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Without this measure, BART cuts could close the Orinda, North Concord, Pittsburg-BayPoint, and Antioch stations, the entire Dublin/ Pleasanton line, and the Oakland Airport Connector.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Severe BART service cuts would ripple across the East Bay, disrupting transit connections and straining transportation options. More cars would flood Highway 4, Interstates 680 and 80, Highway 24, and local streets, making commutes longer and more unpredictable.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-size: 12pt;">The consequences would impact everyone. Failure of the measure would force thousands of people every single day onto our already congested roads and freeways- worsening air pollution, making traffic jams start earlier and last longer, and resulting in most of us spending more time behind the wheel and less time home with our families.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-size: 12pt;">The Regional Transit Measure also invests money directly into Contra Costa County communities, providing funding for transit improvements and road repaving.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-size: 12pt;">The Regional Transit Measure protects the public transit that local residents depend on while requiring local transportation investments</span></p>
<p><span style="font-size: 12pt;">&#8211; with strong accountability and oversight that requires large transit agencies to show cost savings to continue to receive dedicated operating funding. And it does not tax rent, utilities, prescription medicines, or most groceries.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Please join us and vote Yes on the Regional Transit Measure. <a href="http://www.connectbayarea.com/">www.connectbayarea.com</a></span></p>
